I found nothing blocking at this stage, so the verdict is PASS. The browser-dependent criteria (AC3–AC7) could not be run here and are left to the operator stage, as you planned.

```
VERDICT: PASS
CANDIDATE: f101fc559b2bc2c8882e4b8f5de3be3e14261dc7
FINDING sfid-unique-vs-soft-delete advisory: the unique index on sfId covers only the `sfId` column. EspoCRM keeps deleted records in the table and just flags them. So once a Call, Meeting or Task is deleted (Staff and Intake may delete their own), its sfId still holds the index slot, and re-importing that key will hit a duplicate-key error. | evidence: in all four entityDefs the index is `"indexes":{"sfId":{"type":"unique","columns":["sfId"]}}`; the roles give ER Staff/Intake `delete: own` on Call, Meeting and Task | expected: the CRM-006 importer looks up sfId including deleted rows, or restores them, or the index includes `deleted`. Confirm this in AC7 at the operator stage.
FINDING archived-guard-runtime-interaction advisory: I ran the hook only against stub EspoCRM classes. I could not check whether the core Email repository rewrites any of the 30 protected attributes (address strings or link ids) during an ordinary save. If it does, an ER Manager re-linking an archived email's parent could be refused. | evidence: no EspoCRM source or container here (`docker ps` → permission denied) | expected: AC4 at the operator stage also checks that an ER Manager can change an archived email's parent, and gets a 403 when changing its body.
EVIDENCE:
- HEAD: `git -C worktree rev-parse HEAD` = f101fc559b2bc2c8882e4b8f5de3be3e14261dc7. All tracked files match the candidate. The only extra items are two `__pycache__` directories (git ignores them) owned by forgev2-pl and dated before any of my runs. I set PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every run in the worktree.
- Full suite: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/unit` gives "Ran 310 tests … OK", both in the worktree and in a `git archive` copy in scratch. The candidate's tests run on the base tree give "FAILED (failures=9, errors=15)", so the new tests do detect what is missing.
- Mutations (31 single changes, each applied to a fresh copy of the candidate, then the full suite). Every one made the suite fail:
  - hook: dropped `status`; dropped `body`; added `parentId`; exempted every API user; changed the user name; guarded new records; switched getFetched to get; removed the throw;
  - indexes: changed unique to index on Call, Meeting, Task and Email (each separately);
  - fields: added `readOnly` to Task sfId and to sfThreadIdentifier; removed `readOnlyAfterCreate` from Email sfId; set sfId maxLength to 19;
  - meetingType: dropped an option; changed the default;
  - layouts: removed meetingType from Meeting/list; removed dateCompleted from Task/detail; made the Legacy panel open by default;
  - roles: Staff Email edit `own`; Intake Email edit `all`; Manager can read Email sfId; Staff can edit Meeting sfOwnerId; Intake fieldData missing sfActivityId; Import edit `no` on sfThreadIdentifier and on Call sfId;
  - dashboards: wrong team; Tasks dashlet replaced; title changed.
- Hook, executed: `php -l` (PHP 8.4.27) gives "No syntax errors". I loaded the real hook class with stub Espo classes (`hookrun.php`):
  - 30 protected attributes, 30 unique, and each one is refused for Staff;
  - archived email: Staff changing the body → DENY; un-archiving → DENY; parent / assignedUser / teams / users → allow; saving with no changes → allow;
  - status Draft or Sent → allow; a new record created as Archived → allow (the accepted hand-logging case);
  - admin and API user `er-import` → allow;
  - another API user, a regular user named er-import, and an API user `ER-Import` (different case) → all DENY.
  - Check that this can fail: with `status` removed from the hook, the count is 29 and un-archiving becomes "allow".
- ACL table read from roles.json:
  - Email edit is `no` for Staff and Intake and `all` for Manager (the hook still applies to Manager);
  - on Call, Meeting, Task and Email, sfId is read no / edit no for Staff, Intake and Manager, and the other sf* fields are read yes / edit no;
  - ER Import is yes/yes on every one of these fields;
  - no sf* field has `readOnly`; sfId has `readOnlyAfterCreate` on all four entities, plus the unique index.
- Layouts: Call/detail, Meeting/detail and Task/detail (including dateCompleted) end with a Legacy panel set `collapsed: true`. Meeting list and detail show meetingType. dateCompleted sits on its own row under dateStart/dateEnd instead of beside dateStart; that position is cosmetic, as you classified it.
- Provisioning, run through the fake EspoCRM from the tests (`probe_prov.py`):
  - first run: template created, nothing deployed;
  - second run: "unchanged", no write calls;
  - with `--deploy-dashboards`: one deployToTeam call to the Enquiries team with `append` false, and still only one template;
  - a malformed flag exits with code 2.
- gitleaks: `gitleaks dir` on the candidate tree and `gitleaks git` over 57d93eb..f101fc5 (2 commits) both report "no leaks found".
- Browser / AC3–AC7: there is no browser tooling (no playwright or chromium) and no Docker access, so I could not run them. As you decided, they move to the operator stage.
- Processes and ports: I started no servers. Scratch files are only in /srv/CRM/worktrees/.forge-scratch/CRM-005.
```
